### Fitness API — end-to-end request suite
###
### Works with JetBrains HTTP client, VS Code REST Client, or the `httpyac`
### CLI. The @baseUrl variable defaults to the Docker Compose port; flip it
### to the XAMPP one commented below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
# @baseUrl = http://localhost/fitness-api

### 1. Health check (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Register a fresh user
# Response is { user } only (201): registering doesn't sign in. Log in next.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sam@example.com",
  "password": "hunter2hunter",
  "fullName": "Sam Newcomer",
  "weightKg": 72.5,
  "heightCm": 180.0
}

### 3. Log in as the seeded test user
# Response includes { token, user }. Use this token for the rest of the suite.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 4. Save the login token by hand
# Copy the value from the response above into this variable.
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 5. Get current user profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Update the profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "fullName": "Alex Runner",
  "weightKg": 71.0,
  "heightCm": 178.0
}

### 7. List all workouts (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. List only running workouts
GET {{baseUrl}}/workouts?type=RUNNING
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. List workouts inside a date window
GET {{baseUrl}}/workouts?from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-30T23:59:59Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Create a new run
# client_uuid should come from the device. Re-POSTing with the same UUID
# returns the existing row (upsert), so this request is idempotent.
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "d2b8b2e0-7bf6-4d5c-9c1a-000000000001",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "startTime": "2026-09-15T07:30:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 1800,
  "distanceMeters": 5200,
  "notes": "Morning shakeout"
}

### 11. Create a strength workout (with sets, transaction on the server)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "d2b8b2e0-7bf6-4d5c-9c1a-000000000002",
  "activityType": "WEIGHTLIFTING",
  "startTime": "2026-09-15T18:00:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 2700,
  "notes": "Lower body",
  "sets": [
    { "exerciseName": "Squat", "reps": 5, "weightKg": 100 },
    { "exerciseName": "Squat", "reps": 5, "weightKg": 105 },
    { "exerciseName": "Squat", "reps": 5, "weightKg": 110 }
  ]
}

### 12. Fetch a single workout with sets (replace {id})
GET {{baseUrl}}/workouts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Edit notes on a workout (replace {id}) — phase 8c step 7
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/workouts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Felt strong after kilometre three."
}

### 14. Delete a workout (replace {id})
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/workouts/10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Log out — deletes the current token row
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Confirm logout invalidated the token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Register with a duplicate email (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "AnotherPass123",
  "fullName": "Impostor",
  "weightKg": 80.0
}

### 17. Login with wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "wrongPassword"
}

### 18. Create a workout with invalid input (expect 422 + fields map)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "d2b8b2e0-7bf6-4d5c-9c1a-000000000099",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "startTime": "not-a-real-timestamp",
  "durationSeconds": 0,
  "distanceMeters": -5
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Goals (phase 7)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Goals (phase 8b shape: duration_days + startDate; main + extend)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### 19. List goals
GET {{baseUrl}}/goals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 20. Create a 30-day distance running goal
# Client sends its local startDate; server validates it against today ±1
# and computes `lastDay = startDate + durationDays - 1` server-side.
# Response includes `id`; copy it into `@goalId` below.
# @name createGoal
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Run 50 km in 30 days",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "goalType": "distance",
  "targetValue": 50,
  "startDate": "2026-10-06",
  "durationDays": 30
}

### 21. Create a 21-day cycling distance goal
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Ride 150 km in 21 days",
  "activityType": "CYCLING",
  "goalType": "distance",
  "targetValue": 150,
  "startDate": "2026-10-06",
  "durationDays": 21
}

### 22. Create an any-activity count goal (14 days)
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "4 sessions in 14 days",
  "activityType": null,
  "goalType": "count",
  "targetValue": 4,
  "startDate": "2026-10-06",
  "durationDays": 14
}

### 23. Save the goal id by hand (copy the `id` from response 20).
@goalId = 1

### 24. Update a goal (title + target + durationDays)
# Missing fields keep their stored value, so "any activity" must be sent
# as an explicit "activityType": null. A new target, metric, activity or
# span also clears completedNotified (a reworked goal is celebrated again).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/goals/{{goalId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Run 60 km in 45 days",
  "targetValue": 60,
  "durationDays": 45
}

### 25. Delete a goal
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/goals/{{goalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 26. Delete a goal that doesn't belong to this user (expect 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/goals/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 27. Create an invalid goal — distance goal on WEIGHTLIFTING
### expect 422 with fields.activityType
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "This shouldn't work",
  "activityType": "WEIGHTLIFTING",
  "goalType": "distance",
  "targetValue": 10,
  "startDate": "2026-10-06",
  "durationDays": 7
}

### 28. Mark a goal as "completion celebrated" (server flag flip)
### Used by the client after firing the celebration Snackbar once,
### so a subsequent refresh (or a new session) won't re-celebrate.
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals/{{goalId}}/notified
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 28a. Reject: 400-day goal (expect 422 with fields.durationDays)
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Too long",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "goalType": "distance",
  "targetValue": 100,
  "startDate": "2026-10-06",
  "durationDays": 400
}

### 28b. Reject: weight goal on RUNNING (expect 422 with fields.activityType)
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Weight on running",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "goalType": "volume",
  "targetValue": 1000,
  "startDate": "2026-10-06",
  "durationDays": 30
}

### 28c. Reject: startDate too far from server today (expect 422 with fields.startDate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Future goal",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "goalType": "distance",
  "targetValue": 20,
  "startDate": "2026-12-01",
  "durationDays": 14
}

### 28d. Make a goal the main goal (clears is_main on sibling goals)
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals/{{goalId}}/main
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 28e. Extend an active goal by 7 days
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals/{{goalId}}/extend
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "days": 7
}

### 28f. Reject: extend an ended goal (point at a seeded ended-goal id;
### expect 422 with fields.days)
POST {{baseUrl}}/goals/5/extend
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "days": 7
}

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Phase 8a — route points
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### 29. Create a running workout with a 3-point route
### Returns 201. The response.routePoints echoes what was stored.
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "a0e5b3f8-11aa-4cc0-9fe2-000000000001",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "startTime": "2026-10-05T10:00:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 1800,
  "distanceMeters": 4800,
  "notes": "Phase 8a smoke test",
  "routePoints": [
    { "seq": 0, "latitude": 51.5007, "longitude": -0.1246,
      "elapsedMs": 0,    "accuracyM": 5.0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T10:00:00Z" },
    { "seq": 1, "latitude": 51.5017, "longitude": -0.1236,
      "elapsedMs": 60000, "accuracyM": 6.0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T10:01:00Z" },
    { "seq": 2, "latitude": 51.5027, "longitude": -0.1226,
      "elapsedMs": 120000, "accuracyM": 4.5, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T10:02:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 30. Fetch that workout — response includes routePoints in seq order
GET {{baseUrl}}/workouts/REPLACE_WITH_ID_FROM_29
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 31. Re-POST the same clientUuid (idempotency) — route stays as originally stored
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "a0e5b3f8-11aa-4cc0-9fe2-000000000001",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "startTime": "2026-10-05T10:00:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 1800,
  "distanceMeters": 4800,
  "routePoints": [
    { "seq": 99, "latitude": 0.0, "longitude": 0.0,
      "elapsedMs": 0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T10:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 32. Rejected: latitude out of range (expect 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "a0e5b3f8-11aa-4cc0-9fe2-000000000002",
  "activityType": "CYCLING",
  "startTime": "2026-10-05T11:00:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 600,
  "distanceMeters": 3000,
  "routePoints": [
    { "seq": 0, "latitude": 95.0, "longitude": 10.0,
      "elapsedMs": 0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T11:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 33. Rejected: WEIGHTLIFTING workout cannot carry a route (expect 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "a0e5b3f8-11aa-4cc0-9fe2-000000000003",
  "activityType": "WEIGHTLIFTING",
  "startTime": "2026-10-05T12:00:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 1800,
  "sets": [
    { "exerciseName": "Squat", "reps": 5, "weightKg": 60.0 }
  ],
  "routePoints": [
    { "seq": 0, "latitude": 0.0, "longitude": 0.0,
      "elapsedMs": 0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T12:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 34. Rejected: duplicate seq within one request (expect 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "a0e5b3f8-11aa-4cc0-9fe2-000000000004",
  "activityType": "RUNNING",
  "startTime": "2026-10-05T13:00:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 1800,
  "distanceMeters": 4800,
  "routePoints": [
    { "seq": 0, "latitude": 51.5, "longitude": -0.12,
      "elapsedMs": 0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T13:00:00Z" },
    { "seq": 0, "latitude": 51.5, "longitude": -0.12,
      "elapsedMs": 1000, "recordedAt": "2026-10-05T13:00:01Z" }
  ]
}

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Phase 8 — Profile endpoints
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### 35. PUT /me — tightened validation (name 2-60, weight 20-300, height 80-260)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "fullName": "Alex Runner Updated",
  "weightKg": 72.0,
  "heightCm": 178.0
}

### 36. PUT /me — email in body is silently ignored (no 422)
### The returned fullName changes; email stays as it was.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "hacker@example.com",
  "fullName": "Alex Runner",
  "weightKg": 70.0,
  "heightCm": 178.0
}

### 37. PUT /me — name too short (expect 422 with fields.fullName)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "fullName": "A",
  "weightKg": 70.0,
  "heightCm": 178.0
}

### 38. POST /me/avatar — upload a profile picture (multipart)
### Replace the file path with any local JPEG or PNG.
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=FitnessBoundary

--FitnessBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="avatar.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./docs/testing/sample_avatar.jpg
--FitnessBoundary--

### 39. POST /me/avatar — rejected: wrong MIME (text pretending to be an image)
### The server inspects magic bytes via getimagesize(), so this is a 422.
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=FitnessBoundary

--FitnessBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="avatar.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

definitely not a jpeg
--FitnessBoundary--

### 40. DELETE /me/avatar — remove the current avatar
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/me/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 41. DELETE /me — wrong confirm word (expect 422 with fields.confirm)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "confirm": "delete"
}

### 42. DELETE /me — typed DELETE (permanent)
### Only run this against a scratch account!
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "confirm": "DELETE"
}

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Phase 8d — Swimming, Rowing and stored calories
### New optional workout fields: laps + poolLengthM (swims only, sent
### together) and caloriesKcal (any type). Every workout response
### returns all three (null when not set).
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### 43. Create a pool swim: 60 laps × 25 m = 1,500 m (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "b8d0c6a2-5f3e-4a51-9e0d-000000000001",
  "activityType": "SWIMMING",
  "startTime": "2026-10-19T07:10:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 1930,
  "distanceMeters": 1500,
  "laps": 60,
  "poolLengthM": 25,
  "caloriesKcal": 270,
  "notes": "Morning swim"
}

### 44. Create a GPS row with a 3-point route (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workouts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "clientUuid": "b8d0c6a2-5f3e-4a51-9e0d-000000000002",
  "activityType": "ROWING",
  "startTime": "2026-10-18T17:30:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 2460,
  "distanceMeters": 6000,
  "caloriesKcal": 345,
  "notes": "River row",
  "routePoints": [
    { "seq": 0, "latitude": 51.4680, "longitude": -0.2160,
      "elapsedMs": 0,       "accuracyM": 5.0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-18T17:30:00Z" },
    { "seq": 1, "latitude": 51.4700, "longitude": -0.2230,
      "elapsedMs": 1230000, "accuracyM": 6.0, "recordedAt": "2026-10-18T17:50:30Z" },
    { "seq": 2, "latitude": 51.4725, "longitude": -0.2300,
      "elapsedMs": 2460000, "accuracyM": 4.5, "recordedAt": "2026-10-18T18:11:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 45. List only swims
GET {{baseUrl}}/workouts?type=SWIMMING
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 46. List only rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/workouts?type=ROWING
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

